    "body": "## Summary\n- re-read and identity-validate the authoritative Stripe platform Transfer before every live `SUBMITTED -> PAID` Stripe Connect settlement\n- require the Transfer to be completely unreversed (`amount_reversed == 0` and not marked reversed) before local `PAID`\n- keep failed/canceled recovery idempotent: reversal retry first retrieves the Transfer and short-circuits when Stripe already shows the amount reversed\n- close the crash window where Stripe Transfer reversal succeeds but the local transaction rolls back, then a contradictory `payout.paid` event arrives before the failed event retries\n- add service tests proving the provider-state read happens before local settlement and that a reversed Transfer blocks `PAID`\n- add gateway tests for fully-reversed retry short-circuit, pristine paid guard and partial-reversal rejection\n- update payout architecture documentation; no Flyway migration is required\n\n## Financial invariant\nIf transfer reversal succeeds externally but the application dies before committing local `FAILED`, the payout can still look `SUBMITTED` in PostgreSQL. A later `paid` event must not be able to mark that payout paid while the platform Transfer has already been recovered. This PR makes Stripe Transfer state an explicit precondition of `SUBMITTED -> PAID`.\n\nProvider read failure, identity mismatch, or any full/partial reversal fails closed and leaves the wallet reserve held.\n\n## Validation required before merge\n- exact-head API/Maven verify including the new gateway/service tests\n- Worker payout smoke\n- Web dependency audit/test/lint/build\n- Production Compose contract\n- full Containers/runtime smoke\n- unchanged `master`, mergeable PR and exact latest head verification\n\nMerge only with a merge commit after every latest-head check is complete and green.",
